3 Work it out yourself
Move the sliders. Sensitivity and specificity start at the values from our cohort. The numbers recompute in your browser as you drag.

viewof prevalence = Inputs.range([0.001, 0.6], {
  value: 0.13, step: 0.001, label: "Prevalence (pre-test probability)"
})
viewof sensitivity = Inputs.range([0.5, 1], {
  value: sens_in, step: 0.005, label: "Sensitivity"
})
viewof specificity = Inputs.range([0.5, 1], {
  value: spec_in, step: 0.005, label: "Specificity"
})























cohortSize = 10000
diseased = cohortSize * prevalence
tp = diseased * sensitivity
fn = diseased - tp
tn = (cohortSize - diseased) * specificity
fp = (cohortSize - diseased) - tn
ppv_live = tp / (tp + fp)
npv_live = tn / (tn + fn)
lrPos = sensitivity / (1 - specificity)
lrNeg = (1 - sensitivity) / specificity
fmt = (x) =&gt; (100 * x).toFixed(1) + "%"
n = (x) =&gt; Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en")






















































































html`&lt;table class="dtx-2x2"&gt;
  &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Disease present&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Disease absent&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Total&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Test positive&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;td class="hit"&gt;${n(tp)}&lt;span class="cell-label"&gt;true positive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="miss"&gt;${n(fp)}&lt;span class="cell-label"&gt;false positive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;${n(tp + fp)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Test negative&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;td class="miss"&gt;${n(fn)}&lt;span class="cell-label"&gt;false negative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="hit"&gt;${n(tn)}&lt;span class="cell-label"&gt;true negative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;${n(fn + tn)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Total&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;${n(diseased)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${n(cohortSize - diseased)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;${n(cohortSize)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align:center; font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; line-height:1.9"&gt;
  &lt;strong&gt;PPV ${fmt(ppv_live)}&lt;/strong&gt; &nbsp;·&nbsp;
  &lt;strong&gt;NPV ${fmt(npv_live)}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;span style="font-size:0.9em; opacity:0.8"&gt;
    positive likelihood ratio ${lrPos.toFixed(1)} &nbsp;·&nbsp;
    negative likelihood ratio ${lrNeg.toFixed(2)}
  &lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;`






Drag prevalence down towards 1% while leaving the test untouched, and watch PPV fall away. That single behaviour explains most of the controversy around population screening programmes.
